Shift counters strategically at combat with Tidus, trigger Cheer to draw cards and proliferate on damage, leverage Danny Pink for mass card draw, and overrun opponents with unblockable, counter-boosted creatures.

# Counter relocation and Cheer proliferation
Tidus, Yuna's Guardian :: at the beginning of combat on your turn, you may move a counter from target creature you control onto a second target creature you control. His Cheer ability dictates that whenever one or more creatures you control with counters on them deal combat damage to a player, you may draw a card and proliferate. Note that Tidus can move ANY counter type, including shield counters, indestructible counters from Arwen, Mortal Queen, or +1/+1 counters.
Danny Pink :: whenever a counter is put on a creature you control, if it didn't have a counter put on it yet this turn, you draw a card. Tidus moving a counter onto a creature puts a counter on it, immediately triggering Danny Pink. Proliferating subsequently places counters on multiple creatures, drawing fresh cards for each creature modified!
Tekuthal, Inquiry Dominus :: whenever you proliferate, proliferate an additional time instead, doubling Tidus's Cheer payoff.
Inexorable Tide :: proliferates whenever you cast any spell.
Evolution Sage :: proliferates on every land entry under your control.
Sword of Truth and Justice :: grants protection from white and blue, puts a +1/+1 counter on a creature on damage, and proliferates.

# Evasion and counter-scaling payoffs
Herald of Secret Streams :: creatures you control with +1/+1 counters on them cannot be blocked, guaranteeing that your entire army connects to trigger Cheer and combat damage effects.
Kodama of the West Tree :: modified creatures you control have trample; whenever a modified creature deals combat damage to a player, search a basic land onto the battlefield tapped.
Kalonian Hydra :: enters with four +1/+1 counters, trample, and doubles the number of +1/+1 counters on each creature you control whenever it attacks.
Sovereign Okinec Ahau :: whenever you attack, each creature you control with power greater than its base power gets a number of +1/+1 counters equal to the difference, exponentially swelling your team.
Crystalline Crawler :: enters with +1/+1 counters, gains counters on spell casts, and removes counters to add mana of any color.
Walking Ballista :: scales with counters and can machine-gun opposing utility creatures or direct damage to players.

# Asymmetric board wipes and counter protection
Damning Verdict :: five-mana sorcery that destroys all creatures without counters on them, wiping opposing battlefields while leaving your entire modified board completely intact.
Wave Goodbye :: returns each creature without a +1/+1 counter on it to its owner's hand, functioning as a one-sided board bounce.
The Ozolith :: preserves all counters from creatures that leave the battlefield and transfers them onto target creature at beginning of combat.
Resourceful Defense :: catches counters from permanents leaving play and lets you pay {4}{W} to move counters between any permanents at instant speed.
Arwen, Mortal Queen :: enters with an indestructible counter and gives another creature an indestructible counter when it attacks.

# Interaction, tutors, and opening hands
Cyclonic Rift :: premier blue reset to eliminate opposing tokens and blockers.
Rhystic Study :: card advantage engine taxing opponents' spellcasting.
Teferi's Protection :: phases out your board in response to mass exile or global destruction.
Heroic Intervention :: grants hexproof and indestructible to your permanents.
Swords to Plowshares :: premier one-mana creature exile.

Keep opening hands with two to three lands, early counter producers or dorks (Birds of Paradise, Bristly Bill, Hardened Scales), and a card draw payoff (Danny Pink, Fathom Mage). Deploy Tidus on turn three, move a counter onto an unblocked attacker to guarantee Cheer combat damage, and proliferate to continuously grow your army and hand size. Deliver an unblockable alpha strike on Turn 6 or later.
House rules apply: infinite combo loops and compact wins are restricted to Turn 6 or later. Earlier turns focus on establishing board presence, counter accumulation, and combat triggers.